ClusterTrack - License and Usage Notice
=========================================

Copyright (c) Alexandre Matov. All rights reserved except as granted below.

1. Scope
--------
This repository contains C++ and MATLAB code written by Alexandre Matov
for the ClusterTrack algorithm, used for comprehensive measurements of
microtubule behavior, including during stages of depolymerization.

2. Permitted use
-----------------
Permission is granted to use, copy, and modify the Alexandre Matov-authored
code in this repository free of charge for research and educational
purposes, provided that:

  a) Any resulting publication, presentation, or derivative work cites
     the relevant publication(s) referenced in README.md;
  b) This notice is retained in copies or substantial portions of the
     code.

Commercial use, redistribution, or incorporation into a commercial product
or service requires prior written permission from Alexandre Matov
(alexandre.matov@gmail.com).

3. No warranty
---------------
This software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express
or implied, including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability,
fitness for a particular purpose, and noninfringement. In no event shall
the author be liable for any claim, damages, or other liability arising
from the use of this software.

4. Third-party components
--------------------------
Two subdirectories bundle code by other authors, retained here for
reference and comparison, and NOT relicensed by the terms above:

  - GOA_Veenman/           Tracking algorithm by Cor J. Veenman (Delft
                           University of Technology), based on the
                           Hungarian algorithm. Distributed under its own
                           permissive license -- see
                           GOA_Veenman/license.txt for the exact terms
                           (free to use, copy, modify, merge, publish,
                           distribute, sublicense, and/or sell, provided
                           the copyright notice is retained).
  - HungarianAlgorithm_cCode_LAP/
                           C++ implementation of the Hungarian algorithm
                           by Roy Jonker, modified by Alexandre Matov.
                           No separate formal license file is included;
                           see that directory's own README for
                           attribution.

If you are the rights holder of either third-party component above and
would like different terms applied, please contact Alexandre Matov.
